# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment files
#
# Real .env files hold credentials and machine-specific paths and must never be
# committed. Only the .env.example templates are tracked. These rules are
# repo-wide so a new service directory is covered without needing its own
# .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.*

# ...but always keep the templates.
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!*.env.example
!*.env.*.example
